Yeah, that's what I'm wondering. Seems like a low-profile, niche
interest group like this one would be the last group likely to recieve
spam attacks. Still, this newsgroup seems to have its own share of
trolls nonetheless, so it wouldn't surprise me if one of them had a
bone to pick with someone and decided to take out their own
frustrations on everyone else.

It's actually pretty sad that someone would need an outlet like that.
It's even more sad if the spammer(s) are using simple software that
takes all of the effort out of posting mass amounts of crap. It
becomes less of a revenge-fantasy and more of a pimply fourteen-year-
old adolescent rage-at-the-world complex that reeks of old pizza boxes
and unwashed hair. That kind of geek-chic went out of fashion in the
early nineties.

Personally, I find some of the spam posts just as amusing as regular
nethack posts. Every so often the random dictionary the program is
using puts together some funny choices of words and phrases. In any
case, I wouldn't say the spamming bothers me so much as amuses me.



